$ bash tests/fm-self-update-timer.test.sh
ok - a no-progress run writes one quiet line and restarts nobody
ok - a progress run restarts only the mates that advanced and records the pass lines
ok - a live build token skips the whole run with one skip line
ok - the ownerless age-rig holds only a young lock and lets a stale one through
ok - a dead build-token owner is stale and does not block the run
ok - an unconfirmed restart is retried without new progress and cleared when confirmed
ok - the pass's skip reasons are logged verbatim
ok - a failed update pass is logged and exits nonzero
ok - a hard restart-pass failure is reported and keeps the mate pending
ok - restart outcomes are matched against the exact mate id
ok - pass stderr diagnostics are journalled without mislabelling a no-progress run
ok - a recognized skip line on stderr still drives the skipped header
ok - unrecognized pass stdout output is recorded without a skip header
ok - usage and unknown-action handling are pinned
exit=0

$ bash tests/fm-self-update-timer-arm.test.sh
ok - arm installs both units with the six-hour calendar and starts the timer
ok - re-arming an active, enabled timer confirms and changes nothing
ok - re-arm rewrites only changed unit bytes
ok - status reports the timer, service, log, last line, and pending restarts
ok - disarm stops and removes both units but keeps the log and pending state
ok - a symlink at the timer destination is refused instead of followed
ok - arm fails closed on a missing unit template
ok - arm fails closed when the run wrapper is missing
